    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0197" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1518/226–229.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-12-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1054.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith for
                    your information the program<anchor n="1" xml:id="d142-f1"/> of the ceremonies
                    observed on the 2nd instant on the enthronement of His Imperial Majesty the
                    Emperor.</p>
                <p>I inclose also a copy of the imperial proclamation referred to in the
                    enthronement ceremony document,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d142-f2"/> which, like the
                    enthronement; ceremony, conforms to ancient precedents.</p>
                <p>The following day there appeared an imperial edict, copy of which I inclose,
                    reaffirming in emphatic terms the determination of the new Government to carry
                    out in its entirety the constitutional program as laid down by the late Empress
                    Dowager on the 27th August last<anchor n="2" xml:id="d142-f3"/> (see my dispatch
                    No. 1005, of Sept. 12, 1908), and thus finally dispels any uncertainty on the
                    future policy of the new reign.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d142-a1.xml" xpointer="d142-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
